module systems {
  doc "Systems the engine ships as TypeScript: game-level code, listed explicitly in GameDesc.systems like the game's own, so the schedule (and dump_world) shows them and nothing runs that the game did not ask for."
  core cameras

  value cameras List.System "The camera controllers, in order: og.orbitCamera (og.OrbitCamera), og.followCamera (og.FollowCamera) and og.follow2D (og.Follow2D). Each moves og.Camera only while an entity carries its component. List them before the game's systems that read og.Camera: `systems: [...og.systems.cameras, ...yours]`."

  value combat List.System "The combat systems, in order: og.combatIndex (lists every og.Attack) and og.combat (last tick's hits as damage, then each og.Attack's move, links and hit volumes). They do nothing until an entity carries og.Attack or og.Health. Usage: `systems: [...og.systems.combat, ...yours]`."
    guide "combat §1"

  value interact List.System "The interaction systems, in order: og.interactors, og.toggles and og.doors (list each kind) and og.interact (each interactor's focus, hold and use, then plates, then doors and their links). Idle without those records. Usage: `systems: [...og.systems.interact, ...yours]`."
    guide "interaction §1"

  value inventory List.System "The inventory systems, in order: og.containers and og.pickups (list each kind) and og.inventory (places each container's missing slots, then each og.Pickup into the og.Collector inside its sensor). Idle without those records. Usage: `systems: [...og.systems.inventory, ...yours]`."
    guide "items §1"
}

